{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/filters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"filters-faceted"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../api/features/global-faceting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Faceting API"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"global-faceting-guide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Faceting Guide"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Faceting allows you to generate lists of values for all columns from the table's data. For example, a list of unique values in a table can be generated from all rows in all columns to be used as search suggestions in an autocomplete filter component. Or, a tuple of minimum and maximum values can be generated from a table of numbers to be used as a range for a range slider filter component."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"global-faceting-row-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Faceting Row Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In order to use any of the global faceting features, you must include the appropriate row models in your table options."}]},{"type":"code","value":"//only import the row models you need\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n  getFacetedUniqueValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n//...\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  // other options...\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFacetedRowModel: getFacetedRowModel(), //Faceting model for client-side faceting (other faceting methods depend on this model)\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues: getFacetedMinMaxValues(), //if you need min/max values\n  getFacetedUniqueValues: getFacetedUniqueValues(), //if you need a list of unique values\n  //...\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"use-global-faceted-row-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Global Faceted Row Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you have included the appropriate row models in your table options, you will be able to use the faceting table instance APIs to access the lists of values generated by the faceted row models."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// list of unique values for autocomplete filter\nconst autoCompleteSuggestions =\n Array.from(table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues().keys())\n  .sort()\n  .slice(0, 5000);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"// tuple of min and max values for range filter\nconst [min, max] = table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues() ?? [0, 1];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-global-server-side-faceting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Global (Server-Side) Faceting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If instead of using the built-in client-side faceting features, you can implement your own faceting logic on the server-side and pass the faceted values to the client-side. You can use the getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues and getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues table options to resolve the faceted values from the server-side."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const facetingQuery = useQuery(\n  'faceting',\n  async () => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/faceting');\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  {\n    onSuccess: (data) => {\n      table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues = () => data.uniqueValues;\n      table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues = () => data.minMaxValues;\n    },\n  }\n);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this example, we use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" hook from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react-query"},{"type":"text","value":" to fetch faceting data from the server. Once the data is fetched, we set the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues"},{"type":"text","value":" table options to return the faceted values from the server response. This will allow the table to use the server-side faceting data for generating autocomplete suggestions and range filters."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"api","text":"API","level":2},{"id":"global-faceting-guide","text":"Global Faceting Guide","level":2},{"id":"global-faceting-row-models","text":"Global Faceting Row Models","level":3},{"id":"use-global-faceted-row-models","text":"Use Global Faceted Row Models","level":3},{"id":"custom-global-server-side-faceting","text":"Custom Global (Server-Side) Faceting","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [filters-faceted](../framework/react/examples/filters)\n\n## API\n\n[Global Faceting API](../api/features/global-faceting)\n\n## Global Faceting Guide\n\nGlobal Faceting allows you to generate lists of values for all columns from the table's data. For example, a list of unique values in a table can be generated from all rows in all columns to be used as search suggestions in an autocomplete filter component. Or, a tuple of minimum and maximum values can be generated from a table of numbers to be used as a range for a range slider filter component.\n\n### Global Faceting Row Models\n\nIn order to use any of the global faceting features, you must include the appropriate row models in your table options.\n\n```ts\n//only import the row models you need\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n  getFacetedUniqueValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n//...\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  // other options...\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFacetedRowModel: getFacetedRowModel(), //Faceting model for client-side faceting (other faceting methods depend on this model)\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues: getFacetedMinMaxValues(), //if you need min/max values\n  getFacetedUniqueValues: getFacetedUniqueValues(), //if you need a list of unique values\n  //...\n})\n```\n\n### Use Global Faceted Row Models\n\nOnce you have included the appropriate row models in your table options, you will be able to use the faceting table instance APIs to access the lists of values generated by the faceted row models.\n\n```ts\n// list of unique values for autocomplete filter\nconst autoCompleteSuggestions =\n Array.from(table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues().keys())\n  .sort()\n  .slice(0, 5000);\n```\n\n```ts\n// tuple of min and max values for range filter\nconst [min, max] = table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues() ?? [0, 1];\n```\n\n### Custom Global (Server-Side) Faceting\n\nIf instead of using the built-in client-side faceting features, you can implement your own faceting logic on the server-side and pass the faceted values to the client-side. You can use the getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues and getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues table options to resolve the faceted values from the server-side.\n\n```ts\nconst facetingQuery = useQuery(\n  'faceting',\n  async () => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/faceting');\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  {\n    onSuccess: (data) => {\n      table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues = () => data.uniqueValues;\n      table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues = () => data.minMaxValues;\n    },\n  }\n);\n```\n\nIn this example, we use the `useQuery` hook from `react-query` to fetch faceting data from the server. Once the data is fetched, we set the `getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues` and `getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues` table options to return the faceted values from the server response. This will allow the table to use the server-side faceting data for generating autocomplete suggestions and range filters.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Global Faceting Guide\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [filters-faceted](../framework/react/examples/filters)\n\n## API\n\n[Global Faceting API](../api/features/global-faceting)\n\n## Global Faceting Guide\n\nGlobal Faceting allows you to generate lists of values for all columns from the table's data. For example, a list of unique values in a table can be generated from all rows in all columns to be used as search suggestions in an autocomplete filter component. Or, a tuple of minimum and maximum values can be generated from a table of numbers to be used as a range for a range slider filter component.\n\n### Global Faceting Row Models\n\nIn order to use any of the global faceting features, you must include the appropriate row models in your table options.\n\n```ts\n//only import the row models you need\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n  getFacetedUniqueValues, //depends on getFacetedRowModel\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n//...\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  // other options...\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFacetedRowModel: getFacetedRowModel(), //Faceting model for client-side faceting (other faceting methods depend on this model)\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues: getFacetedMinMaxValues(), //if you need min/max values\n  getFacetedUniqueValues: getFacetedUniqueValues(), //if you need a list of unique values\n  //...\n})\n```\n\n### Use Global Faceted Row Models\n\nOnce you have included the appropriate row models in your table options, you will be able to use the faceting table instance APIs to access the lists of values generated by the faceted row models.\n\n```ts\n// list of unique values for autocomplete filter\nconst autoCompleteSuggestions =\n Array.from(table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues().keys())\n  .sort()\n  .slice(0, 5000);\n```\n\n```ts\n// tuple of min and max values for range filter\nconst [min, max] = table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues() ?? [0, 1];\n```\n\n### Custom Global (Server-Side) Faceting\n\nIf instead of using the built-in client-side faceting features, you can implement your own faceting logic on the server-side and pass the faceted values to the client-side. You can use the getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues and getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues table options to resolve the faceted values from the server-side.\n\n```ts\nconst facetingQuery = useQuery(\n  'faceting',\n  async () => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/faceting');\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  {\n    onSuccess: (data) => {\n      table.getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues = () => data.uniqueValues;\n      table.getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues = () => data.minMaxValues;\n    },\n  }\n);\n```\n\nIn this example, we use the `useQuery` hook from `react-query` to fetch faceting data from the server. Once the data is fetched, we set the `getGlobalFacetedUniqueValues` and `getGlobalFacetedMinMaxValues` table options to return the faceted values from the server response. This will allow the table to use the server-side faceting data for generating autocomplete suggestions and range filters.\n"}
